//
// Normative rule pm_ignore_pa (src/priv/zpm.adoc):
//   When applied to a physical address, including guest-physical addresses (i.e., all cases except
//     when the active satp register's MODE field != Bare), the ignore transformation replaces the
//     upper PMLEN bits with 0. This includes both the case of running in M-mode and running in
//     other privilege modes with Bare address translation mode.
//
// Context:
//   U-mode accesses with Bare translation, so addresses are physical. Each access is built at run
//     time from an untagged base with its top q bits replaced by a tag. The expected outcome is the
//     reference transformation of that address: masked (the access reaches the untagged location)
//     or not (a physical address with any of bits 63:56 set, or one with a high bit no RAM has,
//     raises an access fault; a non-canonical VA raises a page fault). xtval rules (supervisor.adoc
//     stval): a fault may write 0; a valid faulting address must be written exactly; an invalid one
//     may be replaced by another invalid address. So a fault on a transformed address that is valid
//     must report 0 or that address, and a fault on an invalid address must not report the masked
//     (valid) base address. A physical address is zero-extended: bit XLEN-PMLEN-1 is kept, not
//     copied upward, so an address whose bit 56 (PMLEN=7) or bit 47 (PMLEN=16) is set stays an
//     invalid physical address.
//
